# The other half of the pairing the README's Scope section recommends.
# Compiled *together with* `test.in`, the way `oldest-tox.in` is: this
# file only has to say the one thing that differs.
#
# NOTE: Merely importing `tox-uv` is not what it does -- registering
# NOTE: makes `uv-venv-runner` the default run env for *every* env in
# NOTE: the process, packaging envs included. So it cannot live in the
# NOTE: lock the `py` env installs: it would silently move the whole
# NOTE: suite onto a different runner and leave nothing running the
# NOTE: stock one.
tox-uv
